  annotation  = {Read 2026-09-27 from the tile.loc.gov OCR. The Republican convention of 3 August 1881 at the Colored Odd Fellows' Hall splits when a Mahone Readjuster faction walks out; the Straightout remainder hears Benjamin Austin, T. B. Pinn and Van Miller deny that the Readjusters had captured the county's Republicans. It places Pinn twelve days before his resignation (pinn-1881) and says nothing of why he left. Filed in sources as
