                 hundred fifty- four", a court order by "the first day of
                 September, nineteen hundred fifty- four", the vote at the
                 November 1954 election - and with one ballot question instead
                 of two: "Shall the members of the county board be elected
                 biennially for four year terms, as provided in paragraph (f)
                 of § 15-351 of the Code of Virginia?" The question on raising
                 the Board from five to seven is gone, two years after it was
                 first offered and never petitioned for. Subsection (f) is
                 rewritten to stagger from the terms expiring in 1955 and 1957.
                 No petition was filed under this act either. The printed text
