                 citizens" (the paper's spelling). Byline S. S. Kerstein. The
                 list includes "a bill to provide for a referendum requiring
                 County Board elections to be held every two years for
                 staggered four-year terms for members"; "a proposed bill
                 calling for a referendum on either an indefinite term for the
                 county manager, subject to removal by the County Board, or on
                 a limited yearly basis with a notice of reappointment to be
                 made at the end of each fiscal year in June or at the
                 beginning of each calendar year in January"; and "Provisions
                 setting up referenda to establish a County Attorney's office,
                 and to delegate to the County Manager the right to appoint
                 department heads". Those became vaacts1952c198, vaacts1952c569
                 and the four-year-term question of vaacts1952c591. Two things
                 are not in the list: raising the Board from five to seven, and
                 anything resembling the non-interference bar of
                 vaacts1952c443. The delegation had been asked to present the
                 list to the County Board the next evening and wrote that it
