  keywords    = {datedintitle},
  shorttitle  = {Act of Feb.\ 3, 1971},
  sorttitle   = {1971-02-03},
  annotation  = {Title begins: An Act to Amend and Reenact Certain Sections of the Code of Virginia to Conform to the Constitution of Virginia. amending and reenacting §§ 2.1-345, 4-4, 5.1-77, 5.1-125, 8-581.1, 8-653, 13.1-400.6, 13.1-519, 13.1-535, 15.1-53, 15.1-276, 15.1-277, 15.1-322, 15.1-324, 15.1-372, 15.1-670, 15.1-674, 15.1-677, 15.1-685, 15.1-850, 15.1-894, 15.1-1061, 15.1-1349, 17-116, 19.1-35, 19.1-346, 21-243, 22-29.5, 22-29.10, 22-151.1, 28.1-6, 30-14.2, 33.1-92, 38.1-54, 38.1-60, 38.1-104, 38.1-133, 38.1-279, 38.1-765, 39.1-7, 54-118, 56-64, 56-338.7, 56-338.71, 56-374, 58-404.1, 58-465.2, 58-597, 58-684, 58-824, 58-953, 58-956, 58-973 and 59.1-92, as severally amended, so as to conform internal cross-references within such sections to the appropriate references to the Constitution of Virginia and to other titles and sections which have been revised and recodified. The County Manager Plan sections among these are §§ 15.1-674 (county board membership and its appointment of the county manager), 15.1-677 (the county manager's administrative and executive powers) and 15.1-685 (the board's authority to abolish offices): in each, the only change struck 'section one hundred and ten' and inserted 'Article VII, Section 4' in its place, the cross-reference to the constitutional provision protecting the popularly-elected county officers (treasurer, sheriff, clerk, commissioner of revenue, attorney for the Commonwealth, and the trial justice or county judge, school board and superintendent) from the Plan's board-appointment and abolition powers. No other text in these three sections changed. Section 15.1-670, also amended here for the identical cross-reference substitution, is a section of a different optional form of county organization (a board of commissioners exercising combined legislative, executive and administrative power, with no county manager named), not the County Manager Plan Arlington operates under. Read 2026-10-01. The section numbers run 674, 677, 685 with
                 nothing between: §§ 15.1-675 and 15.1-676 are not among the
                 sections re-enacted, the recorded negative behind
                 vaacts1962c623. Filed in sources as "legal/statutes/state/Commonwealth of Virginia 1971 - An Act to Amend and Reenact Certain Sections of the Code of Virginia to Conform to the Constitution of Virginia.pdf", pp. 3, 7 and 8 of
                 uva.x030752236, a copy printed in Sally's own browser on
