@report{arlingtoncode6civilservice,
  author      = {{Arlington County}},
  title       = {Arlington County, Chapter 6: Civil Service},
  date        = {2026},
  url         = {https://www.arlingtonva.us/files/sharedassets/public/v/8/county-board/documents/code/ch.-6-civil-service.pdf},
  urldate     = {2026-10-02},
  note        = {Chapter 6 of the Arlington County Code, 27 pages.},
  annotation  = {Read 2026-10-02 and again, in full, 2026-10-03; the copy is
                 the Code as updated in July 2023. Chapter 6 names the County
                 Attorney in sec. 6-14 (noncompetitive service), sec. 6-17
                 (his employees appointed on merit), sec. 6-23 (the Office is
                 a Group 2 office) and sec. 6-30 (its employees are
                 "confidential"). A full-text search of the Code's chapter
                 PDFs on the County's site finds no chapter that creates the
                 office or provides for its appointment; elsewhere the Code
                 mentions it only as an enforcing party.
                 Its authority is sec. 15.2-721; the Board created the Civil Service Commission under it on 15 June 1951 (sec. 6-1). The Manager, not the Board, appoints and removes employees in the competitive service, appoints the Director of Personnel and adopts the administrative regulations (secs. 6-10, 6-11, 6-15); the Board approves the pay plan and the classification system and may not raise or lower an individual competitive employee's salary (secs. 6-19, 6-20). The executive management service, created 15 June 2003 (Ord. No. 03-15), serves at the Manager's will (sec. 6-14). A County employee elected to the Board resigns on taking office, and a department director or an employee of the Manager's or County Attorney's offices on becoming a candidate (sec. 6-23). Collective bargaining runs through the Manager, and an agreement binds the County only after a fiscal impact study, a public hearing and a Board resolution to fund it, subject to appropriation (sec. 6-30). Filed in sources as "government/local/arlington_county/Arlington County 2026 - Arlington County, Chapter 6 - Civil Service.pdf", the chapter PDF as
                 published, saved on 2 October 2026},
}

