                 General (Opinion 09-94, 2009, https://www.tn.gov/content/dam/t
                 n/attorneygeneral/documents/ops/2009/op09-094.pdf) reports the
                 charter makes the mayor a member of the Council with a seat, a
                 voice and the right to vote on any matter, so twelve ward
                 members plus the mayor = 13 voting seats. The city's own
                 recent Ward 2 vacancy procedure (https://www.clarksvilletn.gov
                 /m/newsflash/Home/Detail/3796?arc=5204) has the mayor vote
                 only to break a tie in that one runoff. If the mayor is only a
                 tie-breaker the count is 12. Current charter text on the
                 city's own site was not found.},
