                 residents of at-large cities had half the chance of electing a
                 member that Black residents of ward cities had, as a quotation
                 attributed by its link to Berry and Dye's 1979 article in the
                 Florida State University Law Review (not entered here, its PDF
                 could not be fetched; Tudor and Tremitiere give the same
                 sentence on p. 23, tudor2023proportional); the page gives no
